2026-02-10 22:46:51,708 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document The Difference Between the Nominal Rate of Return and Real Rate of Return

A real rate of return is the annual percentage return realized on an investment, which is adjusted for changes in prices due to inflation or other external factors. Adjusting the nominal return to compensate for factors such as inflation allows you to determine how much of your nominal return is a real return. Conversely, the nominal rate of return strips out outside factors that can affect performance such as taxes and inflation. is relevant
